  "assumptions": [
    "All assets, maintenance schedules, reserve delays, weather windows and service-capacity units are synthetic. No Sceye, Zephyr, ApusNeo, SoftBank or operator fleet telemetry is represented.",
    "The 30-day/720-hour horizon is a deterministic stress fixture and cannot substantiate annual availability or reliability claims.",
    "Each active on-station HAPS contributes one normalized service-capacity unit. This unit is not Mbps, area coverage, payload performance or a radio link budget.",
    "Two capacity units are required for full service; one capacity unit is required for critical service. Delivered capacity is capped at two units for the useful_service_capacity_fraction.",
    "Normal terrestrial fallback contributes 0.3 units and satellite fallback contributes zero. During the regional weather event, terrestrial contributes 0.3 and satellite contributes 0.8; the nested gateway/backhaul degradation event overrides those values to 0 and 0.2 respectively.",
    "The common weather event makes all HAPS unavailable for the declared service region for 24 hours. This is a service-region restriction, not a claim that every aircraft is physically lost or damaged.",
    "The nested gateway event overlaps the final 6 hours of the weather event, modelling correlated impairment of the HAPS and fallback layers.",
    "Maintenance intervals are half-open [start_hour, start_hour + duration_hours); boundary hours must not be double-counted.",
    "The cold spare is requested at hour 144 and is service-ready at hour 156; the 12-hour dispatch delay is synthetic. It is released at hour 192 after the overlapping maintenance interval ends.",
    "The uncoordinated three-node case deliberately leaves a ready fourth airframe undispatched. It is a policy negative control, not a recommended operating plan.",
    "The staggered policy uses the same four assets but plans one 48-hour maintenance interval per platform at a time; crew, launch-site and spare-part limits are not yet modelled.",
    "Weather and gateway events are deterministic and correlated by an explicit parent event. No independence assumption or probability distribution is inferred.",
    "No aircraft lift-class equivalence is implied; lift_class labels are used to ensure a future extension keeps platform-specific dynamics and maintenance owners separate."
  ]
